THUMB-1 ASSEMBLER as - EXACT ACCEPTED INPUT (asm.c)

  as /tmp/foo.s      -> /tmp/a.out (PNX1: 8-byte header + code)
  /tmp/a.out
  Source <=2048 bytes, binary code <=2040 bytes, <=32 labels.
  Two-pass symbol resolution. Instructions are Thumb-1 subset.

SYNTAX
  one instruction/directive per line; label: (may share line)
  comments start @ or ; ; whitespace separates mnemonic/operands
  registers r0..r7 are low registers, sp and lr also available
  decimal and 0x-prefixed hex numeric operands (inspect number())

DIRECTIVES
  .ascii "Hello\n"  string bytes, no automatic NUL terminator
  .byte 65            one byte
  .word 42            little-endian 32-bit word; 4-byte alignment
  .space 8            zero-filled bytes
  .align 2            align next item to four-byte boundary
  Do not assume .global, .text, .data, .equ, .asciz, .thumb
  or GNU assembler macros are supported.

SUPPORTED INSTRUCTION FORMS
  nop                 bx lr
  push {r4,lr}        pop {r4,pc}
  bl label            b label
  beq/bne/bcc/bcs/blt/bge/bgt/ble label
  movs r0, #12       mov r0, r1
  adds r0, #1        adds r0, r1
  subs r0, #1        subs r0, r1
  muls r0, r1        cmp r0, #5      cmp r0, r1
  ldr r0, [r4, #0]  str r0, [r4, #0]
  ldrb r0, [r4, #1] strb r0, [r4, #1]
  ldr r0, [sp, #4]  str r0, [sp, #4]
  adr r2, label      addsp r4, 0
  sub sp, 8          add sp, 8
  svc #0

ENCODING BOUNDS
  8-bit immediates generally 0..255; aligned word offsets <=124;
  byte offsets <=31; sp word offset <=1020; add/sub sp <=508;
  branch target distances restricted by Thumb-1 encoding.
  'adr' requires forward 4-byte aligned target within 1020 bytes.
  Do not use raw absolute RAM pointers in generated PIC code.
  Use labels/PC-relative references and correct registers.

SYSCALL CALLING CONVENTION
  movs r0, #SYSCALL_NUMBER
  arguments normally in r1, r2, r3; svc #0
  ABI details and syscall numbers: /man/syscalls and source
  include/piconix_syscall.h. Never invent syscall numbers.

On error: 'invalid instruction, label or size'. Check exact operand
syntax, offsets, branch reach, line length and 2048-byte source.
See /man/asm-examples for a working minimal program.

EXACT OPERAND WARNING: movs r0, #9 is valid; movs r0, r1 is NOT.
Use mov r0, r1 for a register-to-register move. Validate adr label
position, .align 2, .ascii bytes and .space padding together: adr
requires a forward, word-aligned, reachable address. See asm-debug.
